{"name":"Niche","hex":"#65758f","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"niche","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A cavity, hollow, or recess, generally within the thickness of a wall, for a statue, bust, or other erect ornament.","Any similar position, literal or figurative."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To place in a niche.","To specialize in a niche, or particular narrow section of the market."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/niche"}],"entries":[{"title":"Developmental niche","blocks":[{"text":"The developmental niche is a theoretical framework for understanding and analyzing how culture shapes child development. Developed by Charles M. Super and Sara Harkness. It is theoretically related to, and shares some origins with, Weisner’s “ecocultural niche,” and Worthman’s “developmental microniche.” See also \"evolved developmental niche.\""}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Developmental_niche","wikidata":"Q5266807"},{"title":"Ecological niche","blocks":[{"text":"In ecology, a niche refers to the specific environmental condition occupied by a species or population. Different definitions have been proposed for the ecological niche, though they mainly revolve around describing the relationship between a species or population and its environment."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3d/Flightless_Dung_Beetle_Circellium_Bachuss%2C_Addo_Elephant_National_Park%2C_South_Africa.JPG/330px-Flightless_Dung_Beetle_Circellium_Bachuss%2C_Addo_Elephant_National_Park%2C_South_Africa.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ecological_niche","wikidata":"Q172861"},{"title":"Niche (company)","blocks":[{"text":"Niche.com, formerly known as College Prowler, is an American company headquartered in Pittsburgh, Pennsylvania, that runs a ranking and review site. The company was founded by Luke Skurman in 2002 as a publisher of print guidebooks on U.S. colleges, but is now an online resource providing information on K–12 schools, colleges, cities, neighborhoods, and companies across the United States."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f1/Niche_logo.svg/330px-Niche_logo.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Niche_(company)","wikidata":"Q5146526"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c2/Ifugao_-_2.jpg/500px-Ifugao_-_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c2/Ifugao_-_2.jpg/1280px-Ifugao_-_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c2/Ifugao_-_2.jpg/500px-Ifugao_-_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Grinnellian niche can be described as the \"needs\" niche, or an area that meets the environmental requirements for an organism's survival. Most succulents are native in dry, arid regions like deserts and require large quantities of sun exposure.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AIfugao_-_2.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2a/Scheelhecke%2C_Landwehrgraben%2C_Biberd%C3%A4mme_2020.JPG/500px-Scheelhecke%2C_Landwehrgraben%2C_Biberd%C3%A4mme_2020.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2a/Scheelhecke%2C_Landwehrgraben%2C_Biberd%C3%A4mme_2020.JPG/1280px-Scheelhecke%2C_Landwehrgraben%2C_Biberd%C3%A4mme_2020.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2a/Scheelhecke%2C_Landwehrgraben%2C_Biberd%C3%A4mme_2020.JPG/500px-Scheelhecke%2C_Landwehrgraben%2C_Biberd%C3%A4mme_2020.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&u